/; EXPECT_ERROR: SpawnRequiresFunctionCall
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/; `spawn` queues a call, so its operand has to be one. The parser accepts any
/; expression after `spawn` on purpose — that way a bad operand reaches the
/; binder and reports with a real source location instead of dying as a parse
/; error pointing at the wrong token.
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

var value: int = 42
spawn value
